A||||7||Fierowrecker||Close call, or the ticket is in the mail?||||5||
Z||000000||Fierowrecker||09-01-2001||02:42 PM||||Hey All!<BR>I was testing the front end overhaul early this morning, doing well over 85 through some curves, everything feeling very good!<BR>Made my exit and stopped at the light, when a cute blond pulls up and seems to be saying something...<BR>I can't read lips, and looked puzzled, when I notice a state trooper emblem on her shoulder...<BR>She drove away, shaking her head, I kinda went into shock, as we don't have unmarked cop cars in Michigan, and I would have gone faster if she had chased me!<BR>Guess she didn't like me doing 125 mph???<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/page1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierohoho||09-01-2001||02:56 PM||||I'm going to guess that you were lucky, she's off duty and heading home or to work.<P>Buuuuuuuuuut,<BR>if you do get a tag in the mail I'll bet its for a "basic speed" which is a visual above the posted limit, or a "careless" for a visual well above the posted limit.<P>But I bet no tag just your lucky day.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||04:28 PM||||Hey, Guess what I got in the mail today from the state of Alabama.<P>Titled: Mandatory Liability Insurance Questionnaire. <P>The Mandatory Liability Insurance Act (Act No. 2000-554) requires that the Department of Revenue to select random samples of license plate registrations to determine if the vehicle has liability insurance. The purpose of this sampling is to verify compliance with the law.  failure to prove you have liability with result in the revocation of you,re vehicle registration and confiscation of license plates. Etc. Etc. Etc.<P>Well about a month ago I changed my insurance over to the Gold SE so I could paint the exterior, restore the interior, and generally upgrade the car.<P>I have a PH tag,(Purple Heart) they can't have it, It's the only benefit I've received from Vietnam. they won't even give me one for each (THREE)<BR>I think about the insurance lobby and how they contribute to the election of these fools. Good profit margin here.<P> Here is a state that can't fund education and they spend millions to see if the car in my back yard is insured. Excuse me but ****um!!!!<P>Get a ticket and never leave the house.<BR>I,I've got to end this,I'm getting mad.<P>Cool. I finally made some stars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Insert screw. Extra letter but what the hell! <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||09-01-2001||04:58 PM||||I think your fine, if you get anything in the mail it will probally only be a warning with no fines. I see off-dudy officers all the time yelling at me but I'v never gotten anything in the mail. However, some friends and me were in an 82 Camaro commin' back from a nearby town and some ass in a little Daytona passed us (were going 85mph) like we were standing still. We couldn't stand for that so we took off and raced him. We toasted him, but hung back next to him for after that both doing 130mph. We came up on a construction zone and let off and slowed down a bit, then took off after it passed. About a week later the owner got a letter from the Nebraska department of roads saying they clocked his Camaro at 130mph+ on the highway. Apperantly they had a tape recording the construction zone at night. Thank god it was only a warning....130+ mph in a 55mph construction zone where fines double, that would not have been pretty...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||09-01-2001||11:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>I think your fine, if you get anything in the mail it will probally only be a warning with no fines. I see off-dudy officers all the time yelling at me but I'v never gotten anything in the mail. However, some friends and me were in an 82 Camaro commin' back from a nearby town and some ass in a little Daytona passed us (were going 85mph) like we were standing still. We couldn't stand for that so we took off and raced him. We toasted him, but hung back next to him for after that both doing 130mph. We came up on a construction zone and let off and slowed down a bit, then took off after it passed. About a week later the owner got a letter from the Nebraska department of roads saying they clocked his Camaro at 130mph+ on the highway. Apperantly they had a tape recording the construction zone at night. Thank god it was only a warning....130+ mph in a 55mph construction zone where fines double, that would not have been pretty...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, she was only mouthing the words, shaking her head, not yelling...<BR>And she was kinda cute too!<BR>Too bad I am an old long haired farmer...<BR>Married, kids, grand kids...<BR>At least my car is still fast!<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||09-01-2001||11:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Hey, Guess what I got in the mail today from the state of Alabama.<P>Titled: Mandatory Liability Insurance Questionnaire. <P>The Mandatory Liability Insurance Act (Act No. 2000-554) requires that the Department of Revenue to select random samples of license plate registrations to determine if the vehicle has liability insurance. The purpose of this sampling is to verify compliance with the law.  failure to prove you have liability with result in the revocation of you,re vehicle registration and confiscation of license plates. Etc. Etc. Etc.<P>Well about a month ago I changed my insurance over to the Gold SE so I could paint the exterior, restore the interior, and generally upgrade the car.<P>I have a PH tag,(Purple Heart) they can't have it, It's the only benefit I've received from Vietnam. they won't even give me one for each (THREE)<BR>I think about the insurance lobby and how they contribute to the election of these fools. Good profit margin here.<P> Here is a state that can't fund education and they spend millions to see if the car in my back yard is insured. Excuse me but ****um!!!!<P>Get a ticket and never leave the house.<BR>I,I've got to end this,I'm getting mad.<P>Cool. I finally made some stars.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Insert screw. Extra letter but what the hell! <P><BR>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-01-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Wolfie!<BR>Here in Michigan, you have to have proof of insurance to get registration...<BR>Then you need to carry the registration and the proof of insurance in the car in case you are pulled over...<BR>But if you cancel your insurance, the insurance company has to notify the sec of state you are uninsured...<BR>Redundancy is the name of the game in government!<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||p-did||09-02-2001||12:29 AM||||You'd almost think that she would have to have radar or laser to get you for something..||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||09-02-2001||12:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by p-did:<BR><B>You'd almost think that she would have to have radar or laser to get you for something..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not here, they can still trail you and say they paced you at whatever speed they say...<BR>And you normally loose the case as cops never lie, cheat, steal, do drugs, etc, that they show cops doing on Discovery channel...<BR>Sorry, I am loosing repect for others...<P><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
